# Samut, the Driving Force {3}{R}{G}{W}: "Start your engines! Other creatures you control get +X/+0, where X is your speed. Noncreature spells
# you cast cost {X} less to cast, where X is your speed." (CR 702.179, 613.4c, 601.2f, 118.7a). Five Moxen and a Mountain pay for it on turn 1
# (speed 1); its haste attack makes Bot2 lose life, so the speed rises to 2 (CR 702.179d). Bot2's own Memnite stays 1/1 and its Mind Stone ({2}) still
# costs two: with one Mox it is refused (Samut's discount is only for its controller). On turn 3 Bot1's Memnite is a 3/1; on turn 5 Bot1's Mind Stone costs
# {2} less at speed 2, so it is cast with no mana at all and every Mox stays untapped. On turn 7 Hedron Archive ({4}) is cast with exactly
# two mana from two Moxen and leaves none floating: the discount is the speed, 2, not more.

